Signed-off-by: Weiming Shi <bestswngs@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Simon Horman <horms@kernel.org>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260415204130.258866-2-bestswngs@gmail.com
Signed-off-by: Paolo Abeni <pabeni@redhat.com>

Here is the root cause:
The bug occurs because `slhc_init()` accepts `rslots = 0` as valid configuration (meaning no receive compression) but does not allocate `comp->rstate` in that case, leaving it as NULL. However, `slhc_uncompress()` and `slhc_remember()` in `drivers/net/slip/slhc.c` do not check for a NULL `rstate` before dereferencing it, leading to a null-pointer dereference (kernel crash) when an inbound VJ-compressed or VJ-uncompressed frame selects slot 0. The trigger path is through ppp_generic.c where a crafted `PPPIOCSMAXCID` ioctl (with value 0xffff0000) causes `slhc_init(0, 1)` to be called, creating an instance with no receive state array.

